# Session-written verification artifacts (screenshots, probe dumps, locks).
# These are produced by review/verification sessions, not by the project. Left untracked they
# dirty the checkout, and the mechanical fan-in's ff step refuses to run on a dirty checkout
# (`fan-in-ff-merge: working tree not clean`) — which wedges the landing of EVERY task at once.
# Measured 2026-10-10: ~3h with no task able to land, six ready tasks stuck behind it.
#
# Deliberately narrow. `artifacts/` is a REAL tracked evidence directory — e.g.
# artifacts/live-voice/composer-embedded/*.png are declared deliverables of
# gap-live-voice-composer-embedded-{dual-entry,acceptance-spec} — so the subtrees that hold
# declared deliverables are negated back in below rather than excluded wholesale.
#
# NOT the place for quay's OWN runtime state outside .quay/ (e.g. tasks/.quay-parse-cache.json):
# that set is single-sourced in plugin/scripts/quay-runtime-artifacts.txt and mirrored above —
# adding a second copy here is what that manifest explicitly warns against.

# ad-hoc probe screenshots dumped at the repo root (never a declared deliverable path)
/*.png
# generated screenshots under artifacts/ — everything there is session output EXCEPT the
# composer-embedded subtree, which holds declared deliverables and is negated back in below.
# The three-step nesting is required: git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is
# excluded, so each level up to the whitelist has to be un-excluded explicitly.
/artifacts/*
!/artifacts/live-voice
/artifacts/live-voice/*
!/artifacts/live-voice/composer-embedded
# tool state dirs of other agent CLIs, same family as the .claude/ rule already in this file
/.codex/
# backups of the secret-bearing .env — never meant to be committed
/.env.bak*
# quay's per-goal gate locks (runtime state, siblings of the *.pid.lock rule above)
/goals/*.lock

# The voice relay's LOCAL settings file: a deployment's own prompt / detector / announce phrases.
# `config/voice-realtime.settings.example.json` is the TRACKED template; copy it here (or point
# VOICE_REALTIME_SETTINGS_PATH at it) and edit. The local copy must never be committed — it is a
# deployment's tuning, not the project's defaults.
voice-realtime.settings.json
